TASK 6 – DESIGN CHALLENGE
Campus Event Registration Desktop Application – 
The proposed solution uses a layered Swing–JDBC architecture. Students can register for campus events, while committee members can view registrations, filter them by event and export the displayed records. MySQL stores the data, and SwingWorker performs database operations in the background so that the interface remains responsive.

Stage 1 – Interpret the Problem
1.1 Identify the users
User	Responsibilities
Student	Enter details and register for a campus event
Cultural Committee Member	View all registrations, filter registrations and export records
Application Administrator	Maintain event information and database configuration

1.2 Identify the screens
The application will contain two main screens:

1. Student Registration Screen
- Student ID
- Student Name
- Email Address
- Department
- Event selection
- Register button
- Clear button
- Status message
2. Registration Management Screen
- JTable displaying registrations
- Event filter using JComboBox
- Filter and Refresh buttons
- Previous and Next buttons for pagination
- Export CSV option
- Registration count and status
1.3 Identify the data
Data	Description
Registration ID	Unique identifier generated by MySQL
Student ID	Unique identification number of the student
Student Name	Name of the student
Email	Student's email address
Department	Student's department
Event ID	Identifier of the selected event
Event Name	Name of the selected event
Registration Date	Date and time of registration

1.4 Identify the business rules
1. Student ID, name, email, department and event must be provided.
2. Student ID must follow the institution's valid format.
3. Email must follow a valid email format.
4. A student cannot register for the same event more than once.
5. A student may register for different events.
6. The application must display a clear success message after registration.
7. Invalid inputs must be rejected before inserting data into MySQL.
8. Database operations must not execute on the Swing Event Dispatch Thread (EDT).
9. Committee members must be able to filter registrations by event.
10. The application must support exporting registration records into a CSV file.
1.5 Testable requirements
ID	Requirement	Expected result
R1	Enter valid student details and select an event	Registration succeeds
R2	Leave the Student ID empty	Validation error is displayed
R3	Enter an invalid email address	Email validation error is displayed
R4	Register the same student for the same event twice	Second registration is rejected
R5	Register the same student for a different event	Registration succeeds
R6	Select a particular event in the filter	Only matching registrations are displayed
R7	Click Refresh	Registration table displays updated records
R8	Click Export CSV	CSV file is generated
R9	Load a large number of registrations	Window remains responsive
R10	Database connection fails	A clear error message is displayed without crashing the application


